{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfpn3ppCLCW4xzBscGaDd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Added `reverse` to `src/str.js:11` and a test in `test/str.test.js:17`. All three tests pass.\n\nOne deliberate choice worth flagging: I used `[...s]` rather than the conventional `s.split('')`. Spread iterates by code point, so emoji and other astral characters survive; `split('')` reverses UTF-16 code units and produces broken surrogate pairs (literal garbage output) for the same input. The third assertion locks that behavior in. It costs nothing over the `split` version, so there's no tradeoff to weigh.\n\nIt is still not fully correct for all text, and I'd rather say so than imply otherwise:\n\n- Combining marks detach from their base character — `reverse('e\\u0301')` yields the accent sitting on the wrong character.\n- Emoji built from ZWJ sequences or flags (regional indicators) come apart.\n\nFixing those needs `Intl.Segmenter` with `granularity: 'grapheme'`, which is in Node 16+ and would be a few more lines. I didn't reach for it since nothing in this kit suggests you're handling such text, but say the word if you want it.\n\nThis also leaves `capitalize` as the odd one out — it's still code-unit based, so an astral first character would break there. Happy to align it if you want consistent handling across the module."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_read_input_tokens":22808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":258,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15dfec09-016c-459d-be76-72a6a1d1da1d","uuid":"d9f4cbd0-f8fd-478d-80f3-3ec362a66d65","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:34:13.185Z","request_id":"req_011Cfpn3